sentences.l:
The Master said: “Hui —
he is not one who helps me;
with my words, there is nothing he is not pleased by.”

Yan Yuan died;
the Master wailed for him beyond measure.
Those with him said: “Master, you grieve beyond measure!”

Yan Yuan died;
the disciples wanted to bury him lavishly.
The Master said: “It will not do.”

The Master said: “Hui looked on me as a father;
I did not get to look on him as a son.
It was not I;
it was those friends of mine.”

Master Min attended at his side, mild yet unyielding;
Zilu, strong and bold;
Ran You and Zigong, forthright.
The Master took delight.

The disciples did not respect Zilu.
The Master said: “Yóu has gone up into the hall;
he has not yet gone into the chamber.”

Zigong asked: “Shi and Shang — which is worthier?”
The Master said: “Shi goes past;
Shang does not reach.”

Ci does not accept the decree,
and makes his goods multiply;
he guesses, and often hits the mark.

The Master said:
“I took you to be asking about the extraordinary;
and after all it is Yóu and Qiu you ask about.”
